  "title": "Inconsistent presentation of links",
  "content": "<p>Mostly, the forum converts a link to a post/thread to a “preview” showing the author’s avatar and post title.</p><p>But sometimes it doesn’t.</p><p>Example:</p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/f181ff29-fe4c-4b15-bd6f-e4ff516c237f.png\" /></figure><p>Both of those links came from the menu ‘Copy link’ option.</p><p>Here:</p><oembed url=\"https://community.st.com/feedback-forum-118/own-post-editing-167655?postid=747359#post747359\"></oembed><p> </p><p>In the above case, it was the same both in the editor and after posting.</p><p>Sometimes, the “preview” doesn’t show in the editor, but does show once posted.</p>",
